# Full-Route Resource Embeds

## Context
Resource embeds currently reconstruct compact product and thread previews and cap
documentation inside a special embedded shell. They therefore drift from the
canonical routed resource surfaces and cannot show a complete product, thread,
or documentation page body.

## Goal
- Render the canonical route content for store products, forum threads, and
  documentation inside `resource_embed`, excluding only the global app layout.
- Add an optional shared section max-height control that caps and scrolls an
  expanded section while leaving the default height unconstrained.

## Non-Goals
- Do not add iframe or remote-URL embedding.
- Do not copy resource records into page JSON or weaken source-domain policy.
- Do not duplicate global headers, footers, or app-layout chrome inside embeds.

## Steps
1. Make the three canonical resource routes accept an explicit embedded resource
   identity while retaining their normal route-param behavior.
2. Replace bespoke resource preview renderers with those routed content surfaces.
3. Extend the shared section shell adapter, controls, and frame with a bounded
   optional max height (1-5000px).
4. Add focused tests and update the durable frontend/custom-page/documentation
   contracts.

## Verification
- Run focused resource embed, route, section shell, and frame tests.
- Run the complete frontend test suite, lint, production build, and affected UI
  policy gates.

